@startuml agent-full-flow
' ============================================================================
'  ONE agent turn, end to end — every layer + every decision, top to bottom.
'  Render:  java -jar ../../../plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng agent-full-flow.puml
'  Action colour = the layer it runs in.
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #888888
skinparam ArrowFontColor #5A5A5A
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam activityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam activityDiamondBorderColor #C9B458
skinparam activityBorderColor #999999
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam noteBorderColor #C9B458

title One agent turn — every layer, from trigger to finish\ncolour = layer    MODE = interactive · heartbeat · cron · channel

start

#E8F0FE:**1 · TRIGGER  (driving)**
A turn arrives:
• interactive message (terminal / UI)
• channel inbound (email, …)
• autonomous tick (cron job / heartbeat);

#EDE7F6:**2 · GATEWAY  (presentation)**
Resolve the agent — explicit agentId, else from the session-key prefix;
#EDE7F6:Set RunContext = (agent_id, session_key, MODE);
#EDE7F6:Create RunHandle; run as its own asyncio.Task;

#ECEFF1:**3 · AGENTSERVICE  (application)**
Load session transcript (SessionStore — memory of THIS thread);
#ECEFF1:Resolve AgentSpec — persona · IDENTITY · tools/skills scope · model · version;
#ECEFF1:Select tools = per-agent allow/deny  +  apply_mode
(hide heartbeat_respond / report_outcome outside their mode);

#FFF8E1:**4 · PROMPT ASSEMBLY  (infrastructure/prompt)** — built in priority order:
1  Identity
2  **SOUL / PERSONA** (editable SOUL.md): resourceful-then-ask-ONE-Q ·
   propose+confirm on big/irreversible · NEVER fabricate · careful on external
3  **IDENTITY.md** — who THIS agent is (refines the persona)
4  mode note: HEARTBEAT.md / report_outcome / channel-reply-verbatim
5  Language    6  Tooling (the available tools)
7  **What you are** — organs present (schedule·wake·notify·channels·remember·
   delegate)  ⇒  "PROPOSE an architecture, then confirm"
8  **Skills** — advertised one-line; full SKILL.md read on demand
9  Planning  ·  Verify-before-send (REQUIRED)
10 Execution Bias  ·  **Honesty / no-fabrication**  ·  Safety
11 Workspace · User folders · Date · Project Context · Runtime;

#E1F5FE:**5 · ENGINE LOOP  (infrastructure/engine)** — start the reason → act loop;
repeat
  #E1F5FE:Compact context (ContextPolicy) — send a recent VIEW (transcript untouched);
  #FCE4EC:**6 · MODEL  (infrastructure/llm)** — call the model
  (FAILOVER across models · idle-timeout 120s · request-timeout);
  #FFF8DC:The MODEL decides: emit tool calls, or a final answer?;
  if (model output) then (TOOL CALLS)
    #E8F5E9:**7 · TOOLS** — for each call: validate args → **GuardedTool**
    (timeout · retry · error-normalize · policy [later]) → execute;
    #E8F5E9:The tool does the real work — one of:
    • files / shell:  read write edit ls find · exec process
    • web / UI:  web_search web_fetch · browser · computer · MCP
    • **memory**:  memory_search · remember · memory_get · consolidate
    • **delegate**:  spawn_subagent → isolated child run → result
    • autonomy:  cron · goal · commitment · report_outcome
    • **skills**:  read a SKILL.md  ·  skill_workshop (author one)  ·  update_plan;
    #E8F5E9:Append each result → loop again;
  else (FINAL TEXT)
    #E1F5FE:**verify_answer(draft)** if available
    (NEEDS WORK → keep looping & fix · OK → accept);
  endif
repeat while (more tool work to do?) is (yes — loop) not (no — final answer)

#ECEFF1:**3 · AGENTSERVICE** — persist the final AssistantMessage → session (durable memory);

#FFF3E0:**2 · GATEWAY** — deliver + account, by run MODE;
if (MODE) then (interactive)
  #FFF3E0:Stream events live → connected clients;
  stop
elseif (channel) then (channel)
  #FFF3E0:Last answer → **channel.send(peer, reply)** on the same channel;
  stop
else (cron / heartbeat)
  #FFF3E0:Record the run outcome (done / blocked / failed + detail);
  if (blocked or failed?) then (yes)
    #FFE0B2:**Notify** the user (client-push + durable + email channel);
    if (Nth consecutive failure?) then (yes)
      #FFCDD2:**Auto-pause** the job (failure_alert);
    endif
  endif
  stop
endif

legend bottom
  The DECISIONS live in the model: which tools to call, in what order, whether to
  delegate / remember / schedule, and when the answer is done. Everything around it —
  persona, identity, skills, tools, memory, guards, outcome, delivery — is the scaffold
  that shapes those decisions. Each coloured box is one swappable layer; default-off
  features (memory, sub-agents, channels, failover…) simply don't appear until enabled.
endlegend

@enduml
